<div class="r i2">Cable hole <span class="tp">negative part</span></div>
<div class="r i1 sel"><span class="tp">▸</span>Bracket <span class="k">×4</span> <span class="sw" style="background:#d9d4ca">3</span><span class="s" style="margin-left:2px">1 won't print</span><span class="dt">⋯</span></div>
<div class="r i1">Hinge pin <span class="sw" style="background:#d9d4ca">3</span><span class="me" style="margin-left:auto">mesh errors</span><i class="mk">3</i></div>
<div style="height:1.5px;background:#ddd8cd;margin:4px 0"></div><div class="r ph fold" style="padding-top:3px"><span>Plate 2 <svg width="8" height="9" sc-camel-view-box="0 0 8 9" style="flex:none"><rect x="0.5" y="4" width="7" height="4.5" fill="none" stroke="#6b6659"></rect><path d="M2 4V2.5a2 2 0 0 1 4 0V4" fill="none" stroke="#6b6659"></path></svg><span class="st">Needs slice</span></span><span class="sum">3 objects</span></div><div class="add">+ Add plate</div><div style="margin-top:auto;border-top:1.5px solid #ddd8cd;padding-top:3px"><div class="r" style="font-size:8.5px;color:#a49e90;min-height:0;padding-bottom:1px">Not on a plate</div><div class="r i1">Spacer</div></div></div><div class="cv"><svg sc-camel-view-box="0 0 330 250"><polygon points="165,45 300,112 165,180 30,112" fill="#ebe6dc" stroke="#9a9486" stroke-width="1.5"></polygon><g transform="translate(120,80)"><polygon points="0,12 26,25 52,12 26,-1" fill="#ece7dd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="0,12 26,25 26,45 0,32" fill="#ded8cd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="52,12 26,25 26,45 52,32" fill="#d0c9bd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="18,10 26,14 34,10 26,6" fill="#2b2b2b"></polygon><polygon points="-5,11 26,-6 57,11 57,34 26,50 -5,34" fill="none" stroke="#ec3013" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 2"></polygon></g><g transform="translate(200,105)"><polygon points="0,8 14,15 28,8 14,1" fill="#ece7dd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="0,8 14,15 14,27 0,20" fill="#ded8cd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="28,8 14,15 14,27 28,20" fill="#d0c9bd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon></g><g transform="translate(222,116)"><polygon points="0,8 14,15 28,8 14,1" fill="#ece7dd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="0,8 14,15 14,27 0,20" fill="#ded8cd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="28,8 14,15 14,27 28,20" fill="#d0c9bd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon></g><g transform="translate(180,124)"><polygon points="0,8 14,15 28,8 14,1" fill="#ece7dd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="0,8 14,15 14,27 0,20" fill="#ded8cd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="28,8 14,15 14,27 28,20" fill="#d0c9bd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon></g><g transform="translate(205,136)" opacity=".5"><polygon points="0,8 14,15 28,8 14,1" fill="#fff" stroke="#8f897b" stroke-dasharray="2 2"></polygon><polygon points="0,8 14,15 14,27 0,20" fill="#fff" stroke="#8f897b" stroke-dasharray="2 2"></polygon><polygon points="28,8 14,15 14,27 28,20" fill="#fff" stroke="#8f897b" stroke-dasharray="2 2"></polygon></g><g transform="translate(78,112)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="7" height="20" fill="#d9d4ca" stroke="#8f897b"></rect></g><g transform="translate(20,205)"><polygon points="0,6 10,11 20,6 10,1" fill="#ece7dd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="0,6 10,11 10,17 0,12" fill="#ded8cd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon><polygon points="20,6 10,11 10,17 20,12" fill="#d0c9bd" stroke="#8f897b"></polygon></g></svg><div class="tb"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="note" style="right:30px;top:8px;max-width:150px;text-align:right">copy 4 of Bracket drawn faint: won't print</div></div><div class="cp"><div class="bx"><i></i><i style="width:70%"></i></div><i></i><i style="width:60%"></i><div class="in"></div></div></div></div></div></div><div style="width:440px"><div class="dv-card"><div class="cm"><div class="lg"><b>Always visible</b><span>Same as <a class="dv-oid" href="#26a">26a</a>. A simple object stays one row; there is no assembly level.</span><b>When relevant</b><span>Swatch with slot number on every object and part row, because this job uses several filaments (a one-filament job shows a swatch only where an object or part overrides it). Parts, modifiers, negative parts and support volumes appear when ▾ opens an object that has them, with Orca's type word in grey. "1 won't print" on the object row; the copy itself greys out inside ▸. <i class="mk">1</i> ✎ = intentional customizations (<a class="dv-oid" href="#26h">26h</a>). <i class="mk">3</i> "mesh errors": the one red word, only for a mesh problem. Lock on a locked plate. Not on a plate at the foot.</span><b>On click</b><span><i class="mk">2</i> swatch: the filament menu for that object or part (same list as the chip, <span class="dv-oid">turn 23</span>). ✎: lists what is customized; each line opens its tool. <i class="mk">3</i> mesh errors: the object menu, with Fix model first. A part row selects that part in the 3D view.</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
  <div class="dv-opts" style="margin-top:40px"><div class="dv-opt wide" id="26c"><div class="dv-olabel"><a class="dv-oid" href="#26c">26c</a><b>Folded plates and the one-object case</b></div><div class="opts" style="display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start">
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px"><div class="scn" style="margin:0">one plate, one object</div><div class="dv-card"><div class="pane t" style="height:200px"><div class="seg2" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 26px"><span class="on">Plates</span><span class="">Project</span><span style="color:#5f5a50">«</span></div><div class="r ph on">Plate 1<span class="st">Needs slice</span></div><div class="r i1 sel">Bracket</div><div class="add">+ Add plate</div></div></div></div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px"><div class="scn" style="margin:0">folded summaries</div><div class="dv-card"><div class="pane t"><div class="seg2" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 26px"><span class="on">Plates</span><span class="">Project</span><span style="color:#5f5a50">«</span></div><div class="r ph on">Plate 1<span class="st ok">Sliced</span></div><div class="r i1">Knob</div><div style="height:1.5px;background:#ddd8cd;margin:4px 0"></div><div class="r ph fold" style="padding-top:3px"><span>Plate 2<span class="st ok">Sliced</span></span><span class="sum">Bracket ×2</span></div><div class="r ph fold" style="padding-top:3px"><span>Plate 3<span class="st">Needs slice</span></span><span class="sum">Bracket ×2 · 1 won't print</span></div><div class="r ph fold" style="padding-top:3px"><span>Plate 4 <svg width="8" height="9" sc-camel-view-box="0 0 8 9" style="flex:none"><rect x="0.5" y="4" width="7" height="4.5" fill="none" stroke="#6b6659"></rect><path d="M2 4V2.5a2 2 0 0 1 4 0V4" fill="none" stroke="#6b6659"></path></svg><span class="cz">✎</span><span class="st">Needs slice</span></span><span class="sum">3 objects</span></div><div class="add">+ Add plate</div></div></div></div>
<div class="dv-card" style="width:340px"><div class="cm">
<div><span>The summary line comes from what is on the plate; nobody types it.</span></div>
<div><span><b>One object</b> (any number of copies): its name and the copies on that plate: "Knob", "Bracket ×2".</span></div>
<div><span><b>Two or more objects:</b> a count, "3 objects". Copies that won't print still count.</span></div>
<div><span><b>Won't print:</b> added after a dot, "· 1 won't print".</span></div>
<div><span><b>Lock</b> only on a locked plate. <b>✎</b> after the plate name only when the plate has its own plate settings (plate type, print sequence…).</span></div>
<div><span>One plate, one object: the same rows as any other job, just fewer. Sliced / Needs slice shows here too.</span></div>
</div></div></div></div></div>
  <div class="dv-opts" style="margin-top:40px"><div class="dv-opt wide" id="26d"><div class="dv-olabel"><a class="dv-oid" href="#26d">26d</a><b>Row menus · one per row type</b></div><div style="display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start">
