You caught two gaps in my proposal.

**The folded plate summary is computed, not stored.** Orca’s model holds each object’s instances and which plate each instance belongs to; JusPrin’s workspace projection already groups those instances by plate. For a plate containing one distinct object, we can derive “Bracket ×2” from its name and the **two instances on that plate**. If it contains several objects, “3 objects” is less misleading than picking one name. The count should include a disabled copy, with “1 won’t print” shown separately. The current projection does not expose each copy’s printable state or a complete off-plate group, so those cases need a small extension; the label itself needs no new saved field. [Plate projection](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Workspace/OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:526), [instance membership](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/PartPlate.cpp:2566) Annotation 1

**Orca’s Project information screen shows much more than a name.** When a 3MF contains the data, it shows a model title, author/designer, license, description and preview images; attachments such as a bill of materials and assembly guide; and profile title, author, description and images. It also offers **Edit Project Info**. These fields are optional: Orca shows “No model information” when there is nothing to display. The saved project’s file name and the model title are different facts and should not be conflated. [Orca Project screen](https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer/blob/main/resources/web/model/index.html), [fields read in this fork](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/Project.cpp:100) Annotation 2

I would revise the **Project tab** accordingly: keep the project name/save state for orientation; show a compact model title, author or preview only when present; make **Details** the home for the full Orca metadata, attachments and edit action. Do not reserve blank space for fields absent from the 3MF. Printer and filament presets in Orca’s Prepare sidebar are setup controls, so I would leave them in JusPrin’s existing setup UI.

### What the proposed Plates tab leaves out

| Orca currently exposes | My recommendation |
| --- | --- |
| **Plate state and controls:** lock/unlock; customized plate settings; auto-orient; move plate to front; on some printers, filament grouping. Orca exposes several on the 3D plate itself. [Plate controls](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/PartPlate.cpp:1115) | Add **Lock/Unlock** and **Plate settings** to the plate ⋯ menu, with a small indicator when the plate is locked or customized. Keep Auto-orient available there too. Check where filament grouping lives in JusPrin before deciding whether it needs that menu. This matters because JusPrin hides Orca’s plate corner controls. |
| **Plate context commands:** Select all, Delete all, Reload all, Arrange, Auto Rotate, Delete Plate, Add Models and primitives, Lock, Rename. [Plate menu](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/GUI_Factories.cpp:1696) | Keep Arrange, Rename and Delete in the plate menu. Leave bulk deletion, reload and model creation deeper in the existing context menu rather than promoting them to visible rows. I was imprecise about **Duplicate Plate**: the code supports it, but it is **not in this stock plate menu**; I would not treat it as a required parity item. |
| **Search for a plate, object or part.** [Prepare sidebar](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/Plater.cpp:2220) | Defer until a project is large enough to make the list hard to scan. |

### What the proposed object rows leave out

| Orca currently exposes | My recommendation |
| --- | --- |
| Conditional indicators for **variable layer height, support painting, color painting, sinking, settings overrides, and mesh issues**, alongside printability and filament assignment. [Object list](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/GUI_ObjectList.cpp:405) | Retain the meaningful *conditional* signals, perhaps grouped into a compact “customized” indicator with a clear tooltip or detail on selection. A mesh issue should remain distinguishable from an intentional customization. Avoid six empty icon columns on every row. |
| Child rows for **parts, modifiers, negative/support volumes, settings and individual instances**. Orca’s object-set model distinguishes parts from instances. [Tree model](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/ObjectDataViewModel.cpp:644), [Orca object-set guide](https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer/wiki/prepare_object_set) | Expand the object only when those children exist. My earlier “parts or copies” wording was too narrow: a modifier or negative part that changes the print should also be findable. |
| Direct printable and filament controls, inline rename, plus an extensive right-click menu for instance count, per-object settings, repair, split, mirror, reload and more. [Object menu](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/GUI_Factories.cpp:1450) | Make the conditional filament swatch clickable in multi-material jobs; keep “won’t print” unmistakable. Have the row’s ⋯ invoke the **same context menu** used for that selected Orca object or part, rather than maintaining a short second menu that silently loses commands. JusPrin’s selected-object **More** control already follows that context-menu path. [Current More control](/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Canvas/ViewportToolStrip.cpp:188) |

That leaves a fairly clean resting view: **plate status, object names and quantities, and only the exceptions that change what prints**. The fuller Orca capabilities remain reachable through the relevant row menu or an expanded object.
